\title{The Commitment Interface}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    What a polynomial commitment scheme has to provide, stated precisely enough that a protocol can
    be proved secure against the interface rather than against a particular scheme.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{Syntax: setup, commit, open, verify — and which parameters are public.}
        \li{Binding, evaluation binding, and extractability; which one a [BCS-style](dhsorens-002H)
        compilation actually needs.}
        \li{Batch openings and homomorphism, and how much of a protocol's efficiency depends on
        them.}
        \li{Functional commitments as the generalisation, and why ArkLib separates
        \code{Commitments/Functional} from \code{Commitments/Ordinary}.}
        \li{Multilinear versus univariate interfaces, and the adapters between them.}
    }
}
